technicalExample:
Wrong:
  "order_number": {"type": "string"}      # required, so the model invents one
Right:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "order_number": {
      "type": ["string", "null"],
      "description": "As written in the email. null if none is mentioned. Never infer from history."
    },
    "fields_not_found": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
  },
  "required": ["order_number", "fields_not_found"]
}
Output for an email with no order number:
{"order_number": null, "fields_not_found": ["order_number"]}

WRONG: "risk_level": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 6}
       # stripped by the SDK, validated only after the response returns
RIGHT: "risk_level": {"type": "string", "enum": ["low", "medium", "high"]}
       # enforced: no other value can be emitted
